A rate-distortion pair $(R,D)$ is achievable, if for every $t\ge0$, $B'\in[0,B]$ and $k \in[0,t-B']$  we have 
\begin{align}
R  \ge \lambda_t(k,B') \triangleq I({\mathssf{s}}_{t}; {\mathssf{u}}_{t}~|~[{\mathssf{u}}]_{0}^{t-B'-k-1}, [{\mathssf{u}}]_{t-k}^{t-1}, {\mathssf{s}}_{-1})  ,
\end{align} and the test-channel~(106) satisfies
\begin{align}
\gamma_t(k,B') &\triangleq E\left[ \left({\mathssf{s}}_{t} - \hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t}([{\mathssf{u}}]_{0}^{t-B'-k-1}, [{\mathssf{u}}]_{t-k}^{t},{\mathssf{s}}_{-1}) \right)^2\right]\\
& =  \sigma^2_{t}([{\mathssf{u}}]_{0}^{t-B'-k-1}, [{\mathssf{u}}]_{t-k}^{t},{\mathssf{s}}_{-1}) \le D  .
\end{align}
where $\sigma^2_t(\cdot)$ and $\hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_t(\cdot)$ are defined in~(108) and~(107) respectively.
$\hfill\Box$

Consider ${\mathssf{u}}_{i} = {\mathssf{s}}_{i} + {\mathssf{z}}_{i}$ and suppose the noise variance $\sigma^2_{z}$ satisfies
\begin{align}
\Gamma(B, \sigma^2_{z}) &\triangleq \lim_{t \to \infty} E\left[\left({\mathssf{s}}_{t} - \hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t}([{\mathssf{u}}]_{0}^{t-B-1}, {\mathssf{u}}_{t}) \right)^2\right] \\
& = \lim_{t \to \infty} \sigma^2_{t} \left([{\mathssf{u}}]_{0}^{t-B-1}, {\mathssf{u}}_{t}\right)\le D. 
\end{align} 
The following rate is achievable:
\begin{align}
R = \Lambda(B,\sigma^2_{z}) \triangleq \lim_{t\to \infty} I({\mathssf{s}}_{t} ; {\mathssf{u}}_{t} | [{\mathssf{u}}]_{0}^{t-B-1}). 
\end{align}
$\hfill\Box$
